  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation 2026-2027 EU voluntary contribution to the UN Resident Coordinator System (through the UN Special Purpose Trust Fund, by UN DCO)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;This contract (contribution agreement, CA) is planned to be signed with the UN Development Coordination Office (pillar-assessed under the UN Secretariat) by the end of 2026. However, start date may actually be retroactive (set in June 2026) to link better with the previous 2024-2025 contribution (PC-52170, NDICI CHALLENGE/2025/484-230) without interruption. New CA will indeed represent the 2026-2027 EU voluntary contribution to the UN Resident Coordinator System (through the UN Special Purpose Trust Fund).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Max. EU contribution will be 14 million euros. Sources of funding will be: NDICI-GE-Global Challenges-Partnerships (7MEUR) and the prerogative budget line promoting coordination between the EU and Member States &lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;on development cooperation and humanitarian aid (another 7MEUR). Budget available in 2026 will be 8.963MEUR*, and budget available in 2027 will be 5.037MEUR**.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;*8.963MEUR available in 2026: 7 from prerogative (4 from 2025) + 1.963 from Partnerships (1 from 2025)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;**5.037MEUR in 2027: from Partnerships.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Contract is likely to be signed by use of CRIS as most probably adopting USD as currency of the agreement.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
